      "title": "Extending PID to Behavior",
      "gist": "Known limitations of the cortical-culture studies, chiefly their artificial setting, are partly addressed by a primate study showing synergy patterns shift with ongoing behavioral demands.",
      "question": "Do the culture-based synergy findings hold in a behaving animal, and does synergy track task demands? (one primate study)",
      "sourceHeading": "5.4. Caveats to Consider"
    },
    "n0087": {
      "id": "n0087",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0086",
      "children": [
        "n0088",
        "n0089"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-vjzxxm",
        "spya-j4cy9j"
      ],
      "title": "Caveats to Consider",
      "gist": "The culture-based findings rest on bivariate transfer entropy estimates, which can overstate connection significance, and on cortical cultures rather than living, behaving animals, leaving open how well results generalize in vivo.",
      "sourceHeading": "5.4. Caveats to Consider"
    },
